<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><B><I>Lei Liu, Chief Executive Officer and Chairman
of the Board</I></B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><B>Mr. Liu</B>&nbsp;has served
as our Chief Executive Officer and Chairman of our Board of Directors since September 17, 2009. Mr. Liu is one of the three founders
of Hangzhou Jiuzhou Grand Pharmacy Chain Co., Ltd. (&ldquo;Jiuzhou Pharmacy&rdquo;), Hangzhou Jiuzhou Clinic of Integrated Traditional
and Western Medicine (General Partnership) (&ldquo;Jiuzhou Clinic&rdquo;) and Hangzhou Jiuzhou Service&nbsp; &amp; Public Health Service
Co., Ltd. (&ldquo;Jiuzhou Service&rdquo;) (Jiuzhou Pharmacy, Jiuzhou Clinic and Jiuzhou Service, as well as the subsidiaries of Jiuzhou
Pharmacy, collectively as &ldquo;HJ Group&rdquo;), and has been the executive director of Jiuzhou Pharmacy since September 2003 and the
supervising director of Jiuzhou Service since November 2005. From December 1997 to August 2003, Mr. Liu worked in Tai He Drugstore as
a general manager. From September 1992 to November 1997, Mr. Liu was an administration official of Hangzhou Medical Junior College, his
alma mater, where he was also a researcher and an anatomy instructor from September 1983 to July 1992. Mr. Liu has been a licensed researcher
in the PRC since September 1988. As the founder and CEO responsible for our strategies and directions, Mr. Liu provides great value to
us and our Board of Directors. These attributes make Mr. Liu an ideal candidate to serve as our Chairman.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><B><I>Li Qi, Director</I></B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><B>Ms. Qi</B> is one of the
three founders of HJ Group and is currently the general manager of both Jiuzhou Pharmacy and Jiuzhou Service. From January 2000 to June
2003, Ms. Qi worked in Zhejiang Yikang Drugstore as a general manager. From October 1991 to January 2000, Ms. Qi worked in the Branch
Hospital of Hangzhou No. 1 People&rsquo;s Hospital as a nurse. Ms. Qi is a licensed Traditional Chinese Medicine (&ldquo;TCM&rdquo;)
pharmacist in the PRC and is a graduate of Hangzhou Nurse School. The Board believes that Ms. Qi&rsquo;s knowledge of the Company&rsquo;s
history and day-to-day operations and her experience in the PRC medical industry qualify her to serve a director of the Company.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><B><I>Caroline Wang, Independent Director</I></B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><B>Ms. Wang</B> has been
a member of our Board since March 29, 2017. Since May 2017, Ms. Wang has been an investment manager with Zhejiang Provincial Financial
Holdings Co., Ltd. From October 2015 to April 2017, Ms. Wang has been a project manager with JC Group, a comprehensive industrial financial
group which serves the &ldquo;city management&rdquo;, performing internal audit and projects management for a variety of financial products.
Prior to that, Ms. Wang served as an assistant CFO of Kandi Technologies Group, Inc. (NASDAQ:KNDI), a company engaged in the research,
development, manufacturing, and sales of vehicle products. She was primarily responsible for the consolidation of financial reports and
internal control audits. From 2012 to 2015, Ms. Wang was an audit department assistant manager with KPMG Huazhen LLP Hangzhou Branch,
conducting financial reporting audits and internal control audits for listing companies, as well as providing audit service to pre-IPO
companies. None of these companies is related to or affiliated with the registrant. Ms. Wang holds a master&rsquo;s degree in public
administration from London School of Economics and Political Science, and a bachelor&rsquo;s degree in finance from Beijing Language
and Culture University. The Board has determined that Ms. Wang has the qualifications to serve as a member of the Board given her extensive
financial, accounting and auditing experiences, as well as her English and Chinese bilingual capabilities, which facilitates the Board&rsquo;s
supervision of management.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"></P>

<!-- Field: Page; Sequence: 9; Value: 2 -->
    <DIV STYLE="margin-top: 12pt; margin-bottom: 6pt; border-bottom: Black 1.5pt solid"><P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; text-align: center; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt"><!-- Field: Sequence; Type: Arabic; Name: PageNo -->9<!-- Field: /Sequence -->&nbsp;</P></DIV>
    <DIV STYLE="break-before: page; margin-top: 6pt; margin-bottom: 12pt"><P STYLE="margin: 0pt">&nbsp;</P></DIV>
    <!-- Field: /Page -->

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><B><I>Jiangliang He, Independent Director</I></B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><B>Mr. He</B> has been a
member of our Board since September 4, 2018. He has extensive experiences as an attorney. Mr. He has served as a partner in Dentons China,
a large law firm with a presence in approximately 45 cities in China, since August 2008. From July 1997 to July 2008, he was a partner
in the Zhejiang Jiuyao law firm. From July 1984 to June 1997, he was a professor at Hangzhou School of Law. Mr. He received his bachelor&rsquo;s
degree in law from Beijing University. The Board believes his knowledge and experiences in law helps the Board have a good corporate
governance.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><B><I>Genghua Gu, Independent Director</I></B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><B>Dr. Gu</B> is a retired
physician, professor and published scientific researcher in the field of stomatology. From 2003 to 2013, Dr. Gu was a member of the Standing
Committee of Zhejiang Province Political Consultative Conference. From 2000 to 2009, Dr. Gu was the Vice President of the Women&rsquo;s
Hospital of Zhejiang University&rsquo;s School of Medicine (the &ldquo;School of Medicine&rdquo;), where, in addition to being a chief
physician, professor and researcher, he was also in charge of logistics and financial managements as part of the hospital&rsquo;s management.
From 1998 to 2000, Dr. Gu was the Vice President of the Second Affiliate Hospital of the School of Medicine (the &ldquo;Affiliate Hospital&rdquo;),
where, in addition to his medical, teaching and research duties, he was also in charge of the hospital&rsquo;s logistics. From 1995 to
1998, Dr. Gu served as the Deputy Magistrate with the Shuichang County Government in Zhejiang Province, in charge of the county&rsquo;s
culture, education and hygiene programs. From 1988 to 1995, Dr. Gu was the Head of the Medical Department at the Affiliate Hospital and
was involved in planning and management of the medical department. Dr. Gu served as an oral surgeon from 1977 to 1988 at the Affiliate
Hospital. Dr. Gu graduated from Shanghai Jiaotong University&rsquo;s School of Medicine, Department of Stomatology in 1977. The Board
has determined that Dr. Gu should serve as a director given his extensive medical and scientific research experiences, as well as his
government and hospital management and logistics experiences.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><B><I>Pingfan Wu, Independent Director</I></B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><B>Ms. Wu</B> has been a
member of our Board since October 26, 2018. She graduated from Jiangxi Medical College with a major in clinical medicine. After graduation,
she worked in a hospital for eight years as a physician and an attending physician. After that, she joined Sino-American Shike/GlaxoSmithKline
for 18 years until 2014. From sales representative to GSK China Sales/Strategy Director, Ms. Wu was responsible for the sale of multiple
prescription drugs/OTC products in Chinese hospitals, retail markets, government cooperation projects and mergers and acquisitions. Since
2014, Ms. Wu has been working at Cardinal Health China Pharmaceutical Co., Ltd., which is among the top three largest U.S./foreign drug
distribution companies in China (&ldquo;Cardinal China&rdquo;). She served as its retail COO, responsible for retail channel branding/sales
of the distribution products in China and online/offline business strategy planning and operation management for its Direct-to-Patient
(&ldquo;DTP&rdquo;) pharmacy. The DTP pharmacy is mainly a hospital-side pharmacy and the products are primarily high-value drugs. The
Board believes that Ms. Wu&rsquo;s experiences in pharmacy industry brings the Company opportunities in business development.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center"><B>INFORMATION REGARDING THE BOARD OF DIRECTORS
AND CORPORATE GOVERNANCE</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">Our Board currently consists
of six members. Our Second Amended and Restated Memorandum of Association and Articles of Association provide that our directors will
hold office until the Annual Meeting of shareholders or until their successors have been elected and qualified. Our Board is responsible
for the business and affairs of the Company and considers various matters that require its approval.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><B>Independence of the Board</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">We are required to comply
with The NASDAQ Stock Market (&ldquo;NASDAQ&rdquo;) listing standards, under which a majority of the members of a listed company&rsquo;s
board of directors must qualify as &ldquo;independent,&rdquo; as affirmatively determined by the board of directors. The Board consults
with the Company&rsquo;s counsel to ensure that the Board&rsquo;s determination is consistent with relevant securities and other laws
and regulations regarding the definition of &ldquo;independent,&rdquo; including those set forth in pertinent listing standards of the
NASDAQ, as in effect from time to time.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"></P>

<!-- Field: Page; Sequence: 10; Value: 2 -->
    <DIV STYLE="margin-top: 12pt; margin-bottom: 6pt; border-bottom: Black 1.5pt solid"><P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; text-align: center; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt"><!-- Field: Sequence; Type: Arabic; Name: PageNo -->10<!-- Field: /Sequence -->&nbsp;</P></DIV>
    <DIV STYLE="break-before: page; margin-top: 6pt; margin-bottom: 12pt"><P STYLE="margin: 0pt">&nbsp;</P></DIV>
    <!-- Field: /Page -->

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">Consistent with these considerations,
after review of all relevant transactions or relationships between each director, or any of his or her family members, and the Company,
our senior management and our independent registered public accounting firm, the Board has affirmatively determined that the following
directors and nominees are independent directors within the meaning of the NASDAQ listing standards: Ms. Caroline Wang, Mr. Jiangliang
He, Dr. Genghua Gu, and Ms. Pingfan Wu are independent directors. Mr. Lei Liu and Ms. Li Qi are not independent directors.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><B>Code of Ethics and Business Conduct</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">The Company&rsquo;s Code
of Ethics, which applies to all officers, directors and employees, was adopted by the Board on March 15, 2010. The Code of Ethics was
filed as Exhibit 14 to the Company&rsquo;s predecessor&rsquo;s Current Report on Form 8-K filed with the SEC on March 23, 2010, a copy
of which is available on our website at http://www.chinajojodrugstores.com under the tabs &ldquo;Investor&rdquo; &ndash; &ldquo;Corporate
Governance&rdquo; &ndash; &ldquo;Governance Documents&rdquo;.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><B>Meetings of the Board</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">During the fiscal year ended
March 31, 2023, the Board met twice and took action by unanimous written resolution five times.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><B>Information regarding Committees of the Board</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">The Board has three committees:
the Audit Committee, the Compensation Committee and the Nominating Committee. The following table provides membership and meeting information
for these committees for the fiscal year ended March 31, 2023.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

